  "study_notes": {
    "observed": "Street View from 13th St of the WSW long side and the south end: Sep 2025 (pano Spfk1idrxel-cLsXjCOREg, heading 23), Mar 2025 and Apr 2019 from the same viewpoint. A long beige corrugated shed under a rusty, partly grey corrugated gable roof; its south end is an open canopy under the continued roof, on heavy timber corner posts with a deep header across the gable and an eave beam along the WSW side; the wall set back under it has tall double doors and a barred window beside them. The WSW long wall is plain corrugated metal end to end in Mar 2025. May 2026 aerial (Esri level 19, 2026-05-26): the gable roof, grey with rust toward the south end, and a roofed annex in the middle step of the ENE side.",
    "inferred": "The ENE side and the NNW end have no dated photo, so they stay plain: the two lean-tos and the annex fill the ENE steps with no openings, and the NNW gable is blank. The two personnel doors on the WSW long wall stand where bushes and a trailer hide the wall in the photos; pitches, heights, the canopy frame's sizes and the set-back wall's door and window positions are inferred.",
    "footprint": "Frozen 12-edge ring kept; the 12.69 m WSW strip is the gable shed, its south 4.5 m the open canopy, and the stepped ENE side holds two lean-tos and the plain annex.",
    "m4_canopy": "2026-10-28 M4 re-check: the Sep 2025 photo shows the street (south) end as an open timber canopy under the continued rust gable roof, with the enclosed gable wall set back about 4.5 m; a camera fitted to the eave corner, canopy apex and canopy eaves (rms 1.4 px) puts the canopy front on the frozen south footprint edge, so the last 4.5 m of the shed block becomes an open canopy_s block on timber posts (carport scheme)",
    "fix_20261115": "Owner report 2026-11-15. The carport block was a second copy of the photographed south canopy, put in the middle ENE step with no photo (the 2026-10-28 re-check added canopy_s and kept it); being open, it hid 7 m of the shed's ENE wall and the shed was see-through there. It is now the plain enclosed annex the May 2026 aerial shows there (form unknown): closed walls, no openings, a mono roof falling to e6 under the shed's eave. canopy_s as in the Apr 2019, Mar 2025 and Sep 2025 photos: one 0.3 m timber post at each front corner (a post module longer than the face puts one at each face start; none on the WSW side, where the shed's corner carries the eave beam), a 0.45 m header across the front and a 0.3 m eave beam along the WSW side (parts); the canopy's ENE side has no photo and keeps only its corner post and roof edge. Roof colour, set under neutral lighting at the matched pose and from above: a warm grey-brown of hue about 31 degrees, between the street photos' rust-tan (about 22) and the aerial's rusty south end (about 39; its ENE slope reads neutral grey), so the slope in shade no longer reads pink in game; about 10% darker than the brighter-exposed Mar 2025 photo. Walls and timber unchanged (in game, the timber posts render within the photos' range).",
    "review_20261115": "Visual re-review fixes, 2026-11-15: the WSW long wall's inferred roll-up is gone (Mar 2025 shows plain corrugated metal there, Sep 2025 agrees above the bushes). The set-back wall under the canopy takes what the photos show in place of the inferred roll-up: tall double doors (wooden in Apr 2019; dark reddish brown with a dark barred window beside them in Mar and Sep 2025, whose colours are used) as an entry with a lobby door whose glazing is an opaque reddish-brown pair of leaves in a timber frame split by one mullion, 1.4-3.8 m from the WSW corner, and a ground window with vertical bars in a one-bay range beside it, both placed from the Sep 2025 view. The NNW gable's door and the lean-tos' louvres and door were on sides with no dated photo and are gone. The roof trim (fascia) takes the timber brown of the photos' eave beam and barge boards."
  }
